# A pattern here is matched against the file's full path in the
# build context, not against its name.
#
# Until 2026-08-21 this file read:
#
#   __pycache__
#   *.pyc
#
# which excluded `./__pycache__` and root-level `.pyc` files, and
# nothing else. Every `src/aistack/**/__pycache__` went into every
# image ever built here. `selection-ui:0.4` shipped with two stale
# bytecode directories for façade modules deleted the same morning —
# and because their `__init__.py` was gone while the directory
# survived, `import aistack.selection.engine` returned an empty
# namespace package instead of failing.
#
# `**/` is what makes a pattern mean "anywhere".
#
# The same file governed the build of `aistack-core:0.1.0`, published
# 2026-08-19. That image carries the same residue.

.git
.venv

**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/*.pyo
**/.pytest_cache
**/.mypy_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/*.egg-info

exports
reports/generated
context/bundles/*.zip
